A solid RAR5 archive made with RAR 7.30 whose dictionary size shrinks
between entries:

  rar a -s -md4m -m5 -qo- test_read_format_rar5_solid_window_shrink.rar a.txt
  rar a -s -md128k -m5 -qo- test_read_format_rar5_solid_window_shrink.rar b.txt

RAR reduced the first dictionary to 1 MiB to fit a.txt, so a.txt is
stored with a 1 MiB dictionary and b.txt with 128 KiB, in one solid
stream.

  a.txt: 200000 bytes, a 997-byte block of pseudo-random printable
         ASCII repeated.
  b.txt: 797 bytes: bytes 500..996 of that block followed by bytes
         0..299.

b.txt is compressed as back-references into a.txt at positions beyond
128 KiB, so decoding it requires the window to keep its 1 MiB layout.

